Third-party components

identity-swap.html carries third-party libraries and data, each under its own license, which
governs that component only and not the rest of this software. Their full license texts are inside
the page (each under a "==== <component> ====" heading), and in web/ocr-LICENSES.txt and
web/places-LICENSE.txt:

  - pdf-lib 1.17.1 (MIT), with pako 1.0.11 (MIT and Zlib)
  - PDF.js (pdfjs-dist) 3.11.174 (Apache-2.0)
  - fflate 0.8.3 (MIT)
  - UTIF.js 3.1.0 (MIT)
  - gifenc 1.0.3 (MIT)
  - libheif-js 1.23.5, with libheif and libde265 (LGPL-3.0), carried unmodified as its own script
    so it can be replaced; source at github.com/catdad-experiments/libheif-js,
    github.com/strukturag/libheif and github.com/strukturag/libde265
  - tracking.js 1.1.3 and its frontal-face cascade (BSD)
  - tesseract.js-core 7.0.0 (Apache-2.0), with Tesseract, Leptonica, libpng, LibTIFF, libwebp,
    zlib and libjpeg under their own licenses
  - Tesseract's English model (tessdata_best, Apache-2.0), as packaged by
    @tesseract.js-data/eng 1.0.0 (MIT)
  - zipcodes 1.2.0 (MIT), the ZIP code table in web/places.js
  - the U.S. Census Bureau's and the Social Security Administration's name tables (public domain),
    in web/names.js, with english-words by dwyl (the Unlicense)
  - pdfminer.six (MIT), the encoding tables and font widths in web/data.js
